{"id": "EUVD-2026-59441", "enisaUuid": "bae4deed-575b-3b7d-a0df-e24701524da3", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nASoC: meson: aiu: Validate written enum values\n\nThe AIU HDMI and internal codec mux put callbacks use the written enum\nvalue with snd_soc_enum_item_to_val() before checking whether the value is\nvalid for the enumeration.\n\nReject out-of-range values before converting the enum item, matching the\nvalidation already done by the G12A HDMI and internal codec mux controls.", "datePublished": "2026-08-15T05:57:59", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T18:55:30", "baseScore": 7.3, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:L/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/91797708f99e4a910ab019760069c0a7e00a6fc0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/90703664dbc5a4bf3d84f649404318f3cafdbe69", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8a6d6735e7c02e88841cca1497ff3d8089f2ef24", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/96f5b92d958bc34500500f29fab8e0b908f25397", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0965892cc486ca554d72eeb62d85ccf8d0137a5a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d65adf85477247be04ac86886f8edfaa047b5d4a"], "aliases": ["GHSA-wv7f-69g8-fhc5", "CVE-2026-74294"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.13, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "26a9f48b-2a53-31f1-8ade-a91c9b7ff563", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b82b734c0e9a75e1b956214ac523a8eb590f51f3 <90703664dbc5a4bf3d84f649404318f3cafdbe69"}, {"id": "2b9645cf-9141-3254-9403-a129959abf13", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.158"}, {"id": "2d60387d-b052-33c7-832e-869e7264ed0d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.7"}, {"id": "42fc0dbc-7947-33db-9705-fab750411158", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "46c533dc-0c74-3ddf-a81c-b8c2b5fa7317", "product": {